& [RecoveredNeed]
  + the published wire and no-argument one-shot stdio host are verified but lack a portable machine-readable consumer contract and reusable transcript acceptance receipt
  + the separately owned Scribe application reports dependencies but does not discover build correctness or transport identity automatically
  + consumer instructions must not confuse EOF-bounded single raw JSON with MCP newline-delimited stdio

& [SelectedWorkUnit]
  + add one effect-free safe-Rust consumer contract and transcript verifier over the unchanged published wire
  + define exact zero-argument EOF framing response byte bounds exit disposition fixed public host fault and caller-owned input/output bytes
  + distinguish completed inspection semantic refusal and deterministic pre-dispatch host refusal
  + reject partial stdout unexplained failures extra stderr changed response bytes and all unsupported transport coordinates
  + bind receipts to raw request stdout stderr digests and deterministic wire replay without claiming executable identity or proof of actual process execution
  + ship small exact deterministic request/response fixtures including constructive Unicode success empty page two-page pagination nested refusal and malformed outer input
  + replay fixtures through the actual published stdio executable only in bounded test harnesses with explicit time output and cleanup limits
  + publish concrete consumer instructions and an attributed ownership handoff without messaging or editing another thread's application paths

& [BootCorrection]
  + the isolated AGENTS.md still points to historical ReasoningFramework live authority contrary to the current user-provided Cantor overlay
  + synchronize only that boot pointer and mirrored-memory instruction in D:\crf; do not alter the shared C checkout or historical records

& [Boundary]
  + consumer library performs no I/O and grants no launch filesystem service cache provider model update installation remote or application integration authority
  + subprocess fixture replay is development proof under test ownership and is not a new generic launcher or resident runtime
  + actual application launch policy packaging executable identity and installed Eclipse/Scribe acceptance remain outside this work unit
  + official-rmcp requires a separately preserved and signed successor formation; no MCP authority is imported from the stdio host

